.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp/
.claude/worktrees/

# tmp/ is scratch and must stay unreachable by a commit.
#
# test_progression_audit_contract.ps1 used to write its fixture to <repo>/tmp/,
# and an interrupted run left the copied tree inside the working directory where
# the next `git add -A` swept it in. That happened: 669 files of a
# progression-audit fixture were committed under
# tmp/progression-audit-6c5c3685... at 8dfe8f4, including a 155 KB copy of the
# character sheet frozen at that date. The tool now writes to the system temp
# directory, but the committed leftover outlived the fix and was untracked here.
#
# It was not merely dead weight. Those 669 files were 271 of the CRLF offenders
# that test_line_endings.ps1 found, and a stale duplicate of live campaign state
# sitting inside the tree is exactly the fixture-pinned-to-live-state defect
# (F-018) that the audit tooling exists to catch.
tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
integrations/open-webui/chronicle-open-webui/agents/openai.yaml
integrations/open-webui/chronicle-open-webui/assets/open-webui-slash-prompt.txt
integrations/open-webui/chronicle-open-webui/SKILL.md
